0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 625 [
[(The [mtof] object converts a MIDI pitch value to a frequency in Hertz \050so)]
[(that "69" converts to "440"\051. Microtonal pitches are possible, where "69.5")]
[(is a quarter tone higher than 69 \050or 50 cents higher, so 0.01 = 1 cent\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 570 [
[(The [ftom] object does the reverse. A frequency of zero Hertz is given a)]
[(MIDI value of -1500 \050strictly speaking, it's negative infinity.\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 341 [
[(A dBFS scale is possible if you simply add 100 to the dB input value or)]
[(subtract 100 from the dB output value \050in this case, minus infinity dB is)]
[(clipped to -100 dBFS\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 286 [
[(Finally, [dbtopow] and [powtodb] convert decibels to and from power units,)]
[(equal to the square of the "RMS" amplitude.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
