/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 437 [
[(The [rmstodb] object does the opposite conversion, where 1e-05 "RMS")]
[(amplitude corresponds to 0 dB. Values below 1e-05 down to 0 would output)]
[(negative values \050where 0 corresponds to minus infinity dB\051, but these are)]
[(clipped to 0 dB instead. Note that "RMS" is misleading because the linear)]
[(amplitude value maey refer to "peak" amplitude as well. Also, RMS can be)]
[(equally be measured in dB.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 22 530 [
[(The [dbtorms] object converts from dB to linear \050"RMS"\051 amplitude. Decibels)]
[(in Pd are basically dBFS with an offset of 100! Hence, the typical range is)]
[(arbitrarily set from 0 to 100 dB \050where 100 dB corresponds to an "RMS" of)]
[(1\051. Zero dB, which should correspond to 1e-05 in linear "RMS", is rounded)]
[(down to zero instead. Values below 0 are also rounded down to to 0 \050which)]
[(would correspond to an input of minus infinity\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
